    "situation": "Dispatch has recovered. Three recovery checks were run, and the last two in a row, ending at 25 s, came back clean.",
    "background": "The incident-archive export job took a write lock on cad-db for 7.3 s. Its session was incident-archive-28752, running an export batch INSERT INTO rms_export. While the lock was held, cad could not write calls or MDT terminal reports, so it timed out with 504 errors.",
    "assessment": "The root cause was a lock held on cad-db by session incident-archive-28752 (confidence 0.92). Because of it, call-handling could not enter 9-1-1 calls and unit status reports piled up. The incident commander ended that session itself with release_lock on cad-db, and the checks afterwards were clean.",
    "recommendation": "Find out why the incident-archive export job holds a long write lock on cad-db, and schedule it or change it so this does not happen again. Ask operations to review any 9-1-1 calls or unit status reports that were not written during the outage. Also confirm the interrupted rms_export batch is rerun or completed."
  },
